{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK6DMu9rcVRKXEjk74xk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug: usernames that end with a newline are now rejected. In `django/contrib/auth/validators.py`, I changed the regex in both `ASCIIUsernameValidator` and `UnicodeUsernameValidator` from `r'^[\\w.@+-]+$'` to `r'\\A[\\w.@+-]+\\Z'`, as the issue suggested. The old `$` also matched just before a trailing newline, which is why those usernames got through; `\\Z` only matches at the very end of the string.\n\nThe existing `auth_tests.test_validators` suite passes (22 tests). I didn't add a test for the newline case, since the rules said not to edit test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":18875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159},"output_tokens":219,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ba75c94-736a-469f-b55c-d981248d0b19","uuid":"c3b678fd-8b54-452a-bc16-5f154bf7f4f2","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:43:27.087Z","request_id":"req_011ChK6DMkDokBUH2qFY44Bn"}
